# =============================================================================
# Incident Management Platform - root .gitignore
#
# This repo is LOCAL ONLY. It has no remote and is not meant to get one.
# Its purpose is an undo button and a readable diff of every change.
#
# That second purpose is why this file matters: ~750 MB of build output lives
# under the target/ folders. If those were tracked, every "git diff" would be
# unreadable and the repo would be useless for reviewing changes.
# =============================================================================

# --- Maven build output (~750 MB across 11 modules) --------------------------
target/
# The negations below are inherited from the Spring Initializr templates: they
# stop the rule above from accidentally ignoring a real source folder that
# happens to be called "target".
!**/src/main/**/target/
!**/src/test/**/target/

# --- IntelliJ ----------------------------------------------------------------
# IntelliJ's own compile output at the project root.
out/
# .idea/ holds per-machine state (window layout, local run configs, caches).
# It changes constantly and would add noise to every diff.
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr

# --- Other IDEs ---------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.classpath
.project
.settings/
.apt_generated/
.factorypath
.springBeans
.sts4-cache/

# --- Maven wrapper -----------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: this project uses distributionType=only-script, so no jar exists today.
# The rule is kept in case a future wrapper upgrade starts downloading one.
# mvnw, mvnw.cmd and .mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties MUST stay tracked.
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# --- Secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project reads ${user}, ${password}, ${secretkey} and ${apikey} from real
# environment variables, so there is nothing to ignore yet. These rules exist so
# that IF a .env file is ever added, it cannot be committed by accident.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example

# --- Logs and runtime noise ---------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
*.pid

# --- OS files -----------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- Scratch ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ad hoc scripts and scratch files that are not part of the build.
*.tmp
*.bak
scratch/
